Expected elements: MISSING — transaction age; transaction type in the overview grid; the 'supply an ABI' action.

Three Must-show items are absent, so those are findings #1–#3, all P1, and the rating is capped at 4. No timestamp or relative age appears anywhere. Transaction type is not a grid row, though the raw block prints `"kind": "public-avm-call"`. The Decoded input note says "Supplying an ABI decodes them" but carries no control — a remedy named with no path to it, which in this product's honesty register is the same family of error as a retry that cannot succeed.

I checked provenance independently: it is the `Data` row at the head of the facts grid, badge plus the producer's sentences, exactly one form. No band, and none belongs here.

The page is on-register — light canvas, near-black type, geometric sans, minimal chrome. The copy is the strongest thing on it: every note names its cause and the condition that changes it, and none apologises. The provenance sentences ("the execution trace is real... but it is not the execution of the transaction it is published under") are exactly the tone this product claims.

The brand accent is overloaded, though. Indigo-blue carries the primary button, the `On demand` chip, every link, and the provenance badge, so the one claim about whether these hashes exist wears the page's most ordinary colour.

Fixes: give the ABI note a real control; give provenance a treatment nothing else on the page uses.

Rating: 4/10

